Hi Phil,

I'm wondering if you can provide guidance on the interpretation of sDTF stat when it is positive and negative. I read your paper ("may not make a big DIF" but it is still a bit confusing to me.

The excerpt from your paper says: "Negative values of sDTF indicate that the reference group scores lower than the focal group on average, while positive values indicate that the focal group scores higher."  Based on this statement seems, it seems like both positive and negative sDTF values mean that the focal group has higher values than the reference group on average? I feel like I must be missing something? Thank you!

Jeannie

